1276
00:55:20.660 --> 00:55:24.920
And when we were listening to that clip and I asked you if you chunk your wiffle ball,

1277
00:55:25.100 --> 00:55:26.780
it didn't sound wrong to me.

1278
00:55:26.780 --> 00:55:30.200
You also told me your husband has heard of the use chunk it.

1279
00:55:30.540 --> 00:55:30.820
Yes.

1280
00:55:30.980 --> 00:55:34.820
He grew up all around the country, but his family eventually settled in Texas.

1281
00:55:35.480 --> 00:55:40.980
And when he first got to Texas, he heard someone say chunk it because he had been saying

1282
00:55:40.980 --> 00:55:41.560
chuck it.

1283
00:55:41.780 --> 00:55:45.120
And he was able to confirm to me that both are used.

1284
00:55:45.340 --> 00:55:46.140
Thank you very much.

1285
00:55:46.260 --> 00:55:47.240
And mean the same thing.

1286
00:55:47.340 --> 00:55:47.760
Thank you.

1287
00:55:48.120 --> 00:55:48.200
Mm-hmm.

1288
00:55:55.420 --> 00:55:56.380
Mm-hmm.

1289
00:55:56.380 --> 00:55:58.160
And my social anxiety.

1290
00:55:58.620 --> 00:56:03.120
And we got a letter from Anouk in the Netherlands who said,

1291
00:56:03.120 --> 00:56:04.940
I am 19 years old.

1292
00:56:05.080 --> 00:56:09.840
I found your podcast last March and listened to all the episodes nonstop.

1293
00:56:09.920 --> 00:56:15.020
I also just listened to the podcast you did with Elise Myers, and you mentioned that you

1294
00:56:15.020 --> 00:56:16.500
struggle with social anxiety.

1295
00:56:16.980 --> 00:56:21.840
On previous episodes, you have mentioned that you had anxiety before, but I didn't know

1296
00:56:21.840 --> 00:56:26.040
that you struggled with social anxiety, something that I struggle with too.

1297
00:56:26.040 --> 00:56:31.660
I find it so encouraging that even though you have social anxiety, you still chose an acting

1298
00:56:31.660 --> 00:56:33.440
slash in-the-spotlight career.

1299
00:56:33.820 --> 00:56:39.580
I was wondering if you could share a little bit more about your experiences of what anxiety

1300
00:56:39.580 --> 00:56:42.220
was and still is like for you.

1301
00:56:42.980 --> 00:56:44.760
It's a very thoughtful question.

1302
00:56:45.220 --> 00:56:46.160
It is.

1303
00:56:46.300 --> 00:56:46.900
It is.

1304
00:56:46.980 --> 00:56:48.540
And this is such a common thing.

1305
00:56:48.860 --> 00:56:50.180
I have anxiety.

1306
00:56:50.720 --> 00:56:52.540
I am also an introvert.

1307
00:56:53.040 --> 00:56:57.480
But that does not seem like a good formula for a career in the spotlight.

1308
00:56:58.060 --> 00:56:59.640
You know what I would say?

1309
00:56:59.800 --> 00:57:00.180
What?

1310
00:57:00.220 --> 00:57:02.120
Is that you also love a challenge.

1311
00:57:02.520 --> 00:57:03.000
Well.

1312
00:57:03.100 --> 00:57:05.800
So it's like you gave yourself a personal life challenge.

1313
00:57:06.100 --> 00:57:11.780
It's interesting because my therapist a while back actually said that I picked a very challenging

1314
00:57:11.780 --> 00:57:14.400
profession for a person with anxiety issues.

1315
00:57:14.660 --> 00:57:14.800
Mm-hmm.

1316
00:57:14.940 --> 00:57:20.680
This is also someone who decided one year to never use a calculator and only do all the math herself.

1317
00:57:21.340 --> 00:57:22.840
You love a challenge.

1318
00:57:23.120 --> 00:57:24.060
This is true.

1319
00:57:24.920 --> 00:57:31.480
I thought I would start by defining an introvert because I was looking it up recently because I

1320
00:57:31.480 --> 00:57:36.500
kind of wanted to differentiate between my introverted self and my anxious self.

1321
00:57:36.840 --> 00:57:37.280
Mm-hmm.

1322
00:57:38.140 --> 00:57:38.880
So here we go.

1323
00:57:39.020 --> 00:57:43.900
First of all, I learned that psychiatrist Carl Jung developed the concepts of introversion and

1324
00:57:43.900 --> 00:57:46.200
extroversion in the early 1900s.

1325
00:57:46.200 --> 00:57:53.340
And the easiest way to determine if you are an introvert is by discovering how you recharge

1326
00:57:53.340 --> 00:57:54.460
your social battery.

1327
00:57:55.040 --> 00:58:02.240
So introverts have very low social desire and tend to prefer minimally stimulating environments

1328
00:58:02.240 --> 00:58:05.020
and they go inward to recharge.

1329
00:58:06.080 --> 00:58:09.600
Extroverts are re-energized from being around others.

1330
00:58:09.600 --> 00:58:17.080
So, for example, after a long work day, do you like to recharge by being alone or by meeting

1331
00:58:17.080 --> 00:58:17.800
up with friends?

1332
00:58:18.600 --> 00:58:21.280
Guys, where are we on this?

1333
00:58:21.800 --> 00:58:23.760
Are we, what do we have in our group here?

1334
00:58:23.880 --> 00:58:25.560
Do we have introverts or extroverts?

1335
00:58:26.120 --> 00:58:27.900
Uh, introvert for me.

1336
00:58:28.260 --> 00:58:28.520
Okay.

1337
00:58:29.420 --> 00:58:29.940
Introvert.

1338
00:58:30.080 --> 00:58:30.720
I love being alone.

1339
00:58:32.200 --> 00:58:34.420
I don't believe in introverts, extroverts.

1340
00:58:34.580 --> 00:58:35.760
I think everyone's in the middle.

1341
00:58:36.120 --> 00:58:37.960
Oh, I like that, Cassie.

1342
00:58:37.960 --> 00:58:38.010
You know what?

1343
00:58:38.010 --> 00:58:40.640
I love it when Cassie's just sitting in the corner.

1344
00:58:40.680 --> 00:58:41.620
What are you doing over there?

1345
00:58:41.640 --> 00:58:42.780
I don't even know what you're doing.

1346
00:58:42.780 --> 00:58:44.580
She's doing something with some wires.

1347
00:58:44.580 --> 00:58:45.020
I know.

1348
00:58:45.140 --> 00:58:46.860
It looked like you were doing something with wires.

1349
00:58:47.000 --> 00:58:47.940
Who knows what you're up to?

1350
00:58:48.080 --> 00:58:52.100
You're just quietly sitting there and then we throw you on the mic and you're like,

1351
00:58:52.220 --> 00:58:54.120
I'm going to call bulls**t on all that.

1352
00:58:54.260 --> 00:58:56.000
Just like this quiet power.

1353
00:58:56.840 --> 00:58:57.900
It's so awesome.

1354
00:58:58.700 --> 00:59:00.120
I'm actually with Cassie.

1355
00:59:00.120 --> 00:59:05.720
I love being alone, but I also would love at the end of a day to meet up with friends

1356
00:59:05.720 --> 00:59:08.960
and, you know, talk about our day and sort of commiserate.

1357
00:59:09.100 --> 00:59:10.580
I need both in my life.

1358
00:59:10.840 --> 00:59:11.500
I see.

1359
00:59:12.200 --> 00:59:14.560
Well, let me see if this helps us.

1360
00:59:14.960 --> 00:59:22.020
In 2011, some psychologists named Jennifer Grimes, Jonathan Cheek, and Julie Norum broke

1361
00:59:22.020 --> 00:59:25.880
down the introverted personality into four distinct types.

1362
00:59:25.880 --> 00:59:32.560
The social introvert, the thinking introvert, the anxious introvert, and the restrained introvert.

1363
00:59:33.480 --> 00:59:39.500
I read the four descriptions and I most identified with the social introvert.

1364
00:59:40.020 --> 00:59:47.220
A social introvert is most happy in either complete solitude, Ainsley, I'm looking at you,

1365
00:59:47.220 --> 00:59:50.480
or in small groups in subdued places.

1366
00:59:50.860 --> 00:59:55.880
A social introvert will happily go on a solo date or vacation.

1367
00:59:56.660 --> 01:00:02.340
I'll have you know, I was going to the movies by myself as a high school senior on a Friday

1368
01:00:02.340 --> 01:00:02.720
night.

1369
01:00:02.980 --> 01:00:05.560
You still enjoy going to the movies by yourself.

1370
01:00:05.560 --> 01:00:09.820
It's something we've talked about because I would never want to do that.

1371
01:00:10.000 --> 01:00:12.120
Like, I never want to go to the movie by myself.

1372
01:00:12.260 --> 01:00:14.480
I will go eat a meal alone in a restaurant.

1373
01:00:14.660 --> 01:00:15.460
I had...

1374
01:00:15.460 --> 01:00:16.080
Table for one.

1375
01:00:16.080 --> 01:00:20.600
I had to get used to that and it was really hard for me when I was on that show in Vancouver.

1376
01:00:20.960 --> 01:00:24.060
I ate alone a lot and at first I was like, oh no.

1377
01:00:24.320 --> 01:00:25.580
And then I began to love it.

1378
01:00:26.380 --> 01:00:27.360
All right, moving on.

1379
01:00:27.480 --> 01:00:34.020
A thinking introvert are most at peace when they're studying, reading, learning, researching,

1380
01:00:34.020 --> 01:00:35.140
or investigating.

1381
01:00:35.620 --> 01:00:36.580
That's kind of you.

1382
01:00:37.200 --> 01:00:42.420
You love your morning cup of coffee in your office where you can dig into work and...

1383
01:00:42.420 --> 01:00:44.720
I'm telling you, I am every one of these introverts.

1384
01:00:45.140 --> 01:00:49.860
A restrained introvert moves at a slower pace.

1385
01:00:50.160 --> 01:00:51.720
They crave structure.

1386
01:00:52.280 --> 01:00:56.120
And they also have their guard up around others until they get to know them.

1387
01:00:56.680 --> 01:00:58.320
Am I still describing myself?

1388
01:00:58.460 --> 01:00:58.700
Yes.

1389
01:00:58.840 --> 01:00:59.600
I believe I am.

1390
01:01:00.080 --> 01:01:03.820
Finally, an anxious introvert are often quite shy and nervous.

1391
01:01:04.120 --> 01:01:10.500
And when they meet people, they can sometimes appear highly avoidant or even rude because social

1392
01:01:10.500 --> 01:01:15.740
interactions make them so uncomfortable and they want to avoid social interactions at all costs.

1393
01:01:16.180 --> 01:01:18.400
So those are our list of introverts.

1394
01:01:18.400 --> 01:01:21.000
But here's a little bit about social anxiety.

1395
01:01:21.980 --> 01:01:27.440
Social anxiety is a disorder in which you have an irrational fear of social interactions.

1396
01:01:28.020 --> 01:01:30.680
Kind of leans into that anxious introvert.

1397
01:01:31.460 --> 01:01:37.220
Symptoms of social anxiety include excess fear of being judged, not mild fear.

1398
01:01:37.220 --> 01:01:43.680
I want everyone to understand as a person with social anxiety, the key word here is irrational,

1399
01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:51.780
excessive, also intense worry about embarrassment or humiliation or concern about offending another

1400
01:01:51.780 --> 01:01:52.300
person.

1401
01:01:53.120 --> 01:02:00.820
So I will say for me, I can go to a dinner party or a social interaction and on paper, everything

1402
01:02:00.820 --> 01:02:01.420
went great.

1403
01:02:01.680 --> 01:02:04.160
I always know what I'm going to get the next day with you.

1404
01:02:04.160 --> 01:02:09.360
So I get a voicemail where you spiral.

1405
01:02:10.020 --> 01:02:12.580
Yeah, it's really amazing.

1406
01:02:12.800 --> 01:02:14.460
Actually, I can come home.

1407
01:02:14.560 --> 01:02:16.260
I will review every moment in my head.

1408
01:02:16.400 --> 01:02:20.700
I will think of all the ways I messed up, embarrassed myself, offended someone, my heart

1409
01:02:20.700 --> 01:02:21.240
will race.

1410
01:02:21.500 --> 01:02:24.140
I will lose sleep, sometimes for days.

1411
01:02:24.620 --> 01:02:27.620
And this has been going on for me for as long as I can remember.

1412
01:02:27.780 --> 01:02:29.120
I have always had this.

1413
01:02:29.560 --> 01:02:32.140
I've gone to therapy for it, which has helped a ton.

1414
01:02:32.140 --> 01:02:36.180
And I did that therapy before I became a professional actor.

1415
01:02:36.340 --> 01:02:38.180
So I'm very grateful for that.

1416
01:02:38.340 --> 01:02:40.680
I started therapy in my early 20s.

1417
01:02:41.740 --> 01:02:47.780
But I have to say, Anouk, in answer to your question, acting has always been a little bit

1418
01:02:47.780 --> 01:02:48.760
of an escape for me.

1419
01:02:49.380 --> 01:02:52.160
In high school, like I said, I would avoid going to parties.

1420
01:02:52.740 --> 01:02:55.340
But I loved being part of theater productions.

1421
01:02:55.780 --> 01:02:57.560
I loved the artistic community.

1422
01:02:57.840 --> 01:02:59.240
I felt safe there.

1423
01:02:59.400 --> 01:03:01.320
It's a very accepting group of folks.

1424
01:03:01.320 --> 01:03:02.120
It is.

1425
01:03:02.240 --> 01:03:07.320
And I often do well socially when there's a project involved, when we all have something

1426
01:03:07.320 --> 01:03:09.060
we're working on or working toward.

1427
01:03:09.700 --> 01:03:13.220
Because I do like people, and I like being around people.

1428
01:03:13.420 --> 01:03:16.260
And you're goal-oriented, so it's like you have that common goal.

1429
01:03:16.540 --> 01:03:23.240
So while I love acting, the part that has been hardest for me has been the public events

1430
01:03:23.240 --> 01:03:28.800
like interviews or red carpets, things like that.

1431
01:03:28.800 --> 01:03:34.660
But I wrote in our book, The Office BFFs, that Melora, who plays Jan, was a really great

1432
01:03:34.660 --> 01:03:39.700
mentor for me and how to navigate that part of the business with boundaries and self-care.

1433
01:03:40.240 --> 01:03:44.540
You know, it just requires a lot of thought, a lot of strategy for me.

1434
01:03:45.000 --> 01:03:48.260
But yeah, this anxiety has never gone away.

1435
01:03:48.440 --> 01:03:50.240
It just ebbs and flows.

1436
01:03:50.240 --> 01:03:52.580
But here you are, crushing it, lady.

1437
01:03:52.780 --> 01:03:53.300
Here I am.

1438
01:03:53.360 --> 01:03:55.620
Listen, like you said, I'm also very stubborn.

1439
01:03:55.800 --> 01:03:56.860
I don't like to be stopped.

1440
01:03:57.160 --> 01:04:04.040
So I am a stubborn social introvert with social anxiety and an actor and a podcaster.

1441
01:04:04.320 --> 01:04:05.600
And a mom and a friend.

1442
01:04:05.820 --> 01:04:11.940
And I have the best BFF because having someone who will listen to me spiral the morning after

1443
01:04:11.940 --> 01:04:14.800
a dinner party, that helps a lot.

1444
01:04:14.800 --> 01:04:16.840
So thank you, lady, for being there for me.

1445
01:04:17.240 --> 01:04:18.040
I always will.

1446
01:04:18.700 --> 01:04:22.400
Now, Angela Anuk also had a question for you, which is this.

1447
01:04:22.840 --> 01:04:25.860
I know that Angela has shared that she grew up in Indonesia.

1448
01:04:26.140 --> 01:04:32.160
And as a TCK myself, I was wondering if she could share some of her experiences and difficulties

1449
01:04:32.160 --> 01:04:36.100
in growing up there and what it was like returning to the U.S.

1450
01:04:36.200 --> 01:04:39.060
and if and how it has affected her identity.

1451
01:04:39.440 --> 01:04:40.240
Oh, my goodness.

1452
01:04:40.500 --> 01:04:44.680
Anuk, first of all, I think I went into comedy because we move so much.

1453
01:04:44.800 --> 01:04:46.780
And I was such a fish out of water growing up.

1454
01:04:46.900 --> 01:04:51.720
And the quickest way for me to fit in was to make everyone laugh.

1455
01:04:52.100 --> 01:04:55.240
But TCK means a third cultural kid.

1456
01:04:55.860 --> 01:04:58.660
And you grow up not in your home country.

1457
01:04:59.160 --> 01:05:03.560
And you have a hard time kind of figuring out where you fit in.

1458
01:05:03.680 --> 01:05:09.120
Because there's a huge part of me that loves and identifies with my childhood in Jakarta.

1459
01:05:09.120 --> 01:05:16.160
And when I came to the U.S., I found it hard to fit in and find other people who had had an experience like that.

1460
01:05:17.660 --> 01:05:23.020
But yet my family, my parents who were raising me in this other country,

1461
01:05:23.300 --> 01:05:26.980
had all of their traditions from their culture and where they grew up.

1462
01:05:26.980 --> 01:05:34.040
And when I would go to Texas and Louisiana in the summers and I wouldn't understand pop cultural references

1463
01:05:34.040 --> 01:05:39.600
or I wouldn't understand colloquialisms or I felt like out of place there too.

1464
01:05:39.840 --> 01:05:42.140
And it was sort of like, where do I fit in?

1465
01:05:42.340 --> 01:05:48.620
And then you have this small group of people who also grew up like you that you really hold tight and dear.

1466
01:05:48.620 --> 01:05:52.820
I am still friends with my friends that I grew up with in Jakarta.

1467
01:05:53.060 --> 01:05:54.960
We all moved and got dispersed.

1468
01:05:55.250 --> 01:05:56.760
And that's another thing.

1469
01:05:56.940 --> 01:06:03.700
Because you don't have that constant touchstone of that neighborhood you always go home to,

1470
01:06:03.980 --> 01:06:07.600
that corner store, that coffee shop.

1471
01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:10.440
You grow up kind of displaced a little bit.

1472
01:06:10.940 --> 01:06:14.200
And it makes me crave roots and tradition.

1473
01:06:14.660 --> 01:06:18.520
I get very attached to the smallest things about family tradition.

1474
01:06:18.740 --> 01:06:19.820
Like, okay, it's Christmas Eve.

1475
01:06:19.820 --> 01:06:21.480
We open one gift on Christmas Eve.

1476
01:06:21.640 --> 01:06:24.780
And I remember one year my mom was like, what if we just open all of them?

1477
01:06:24.880 --> 01:06:25.680
And I was like, no!

1478
01:06:26.400 --> 01:06:29.420
Because I needed some type of roots.

1479
01:06:31.220 --> 01:06:36.100
But I am thankful for my childhood because I really believe, and I know this,

1480
01:06:36.300 --> 01:06:40.180
that you could drop me anywhere and I will find a way to survive.

1481
01:06:40.180 --> 01:06:41.320
I'll find my people.

1482
01:06:41.320 --> 01:06:43.640
I'll find out what to do there.

1483
01:06:43.780 --> 01:06:44.360
And I'll be okay.

1484
01:06:45.380 --> 01:06:45.600
Yeah.

1485
01:06:45.720 --> 01:06:51.500
I'm not fearful at all about new places and new experiences and new people and new cultures.

1486
01:06:51.720 --> 01:06:53.400
I get excited about it.

1487
01:06:53.540 --> 01:06:53.860
Mm-hmm.

1488
01:06:54.440 --> 01:06:57.400
But yeah, Anouk, I can definitely relate to that.

1489
01:06:57.580 --> 01:07:01.240
And ultimately now, as an adult, I see it as a gift.

1490
01:07:01.240 --> 01:07:04.880
But when I was a kid and we moved back in middle school, that was a tough time.

1491
01:07:05.100 --> 01:07:06.740
And middle school is already tough.

1492
01:07:06.860 --> 01:07:07.480
Oh, my God.

1493
01:07:07.480 --> 01:07:08.320
It's like, what?

1494
01:07:08.460 --> 01:07:09.820
Am I wearing a training bra?

1495
01:07:09.820 --> 01:07:11.600
Oh, what's happening?

1496
01:07:12.000 --> 01:07:15.300
The most miserable couple years of my life for middle school.

1497
01:07:15.320 --> 01:07:15.820
I know.

1498
01:07:16.000 --> 01:07:17.580
And I can still feel them.

1499
01:07:17.840 --> 01:07:25.780
So for you to be also new, not just new school or new kid, but like new to being back in the country.

1500
01:07:26.000 --> 01:07:26.320
Yeah.

1501
01:07:26.580 --> 01:07:26.840
Wow.

1502
01:07:26.840 --> 01:07:26.890
Wow.

1503
01:07:27.480 --> 01:07:28.000
I know.

1504
01:07:28.140 --> 01:07:31.120
I would say things, too, and people would be like, what are you talking about?

1505
01:07:31.280 --> 01:07:31.680
Mm-hmm.

1506
01:07:31.820 --> 01:07:32.480
All the time.

1507
01:07:32.780 --> 01:07:34.940
But Anouk, thanks so much for asking about that.

1508
01:07:35.040 --> 01:07:37.280
It's a part of my childhood that I just treasure.

1509
01:07:37.680 --> 01:07:43.700
As an adult, I really have seen it now to be such a gift that I had, that I grew up in a different country.

1510
01:07:43.700 --> 01:07:50.240
I have such great perspective and appreciation for sort of a global view of the world, that we're all in this together.

1511
01:07:50.240 --> 01:07:51.220
We really are.

1512
01:07:51.640 --> 01:07:54.220
So I love it when people reach out to me about that.

1513
01:07:54.440 --> 01:08:00.480
I also got a letter from Sarah, who is living near my old school in South Jakarta.

1514
01:08:00.480 --> 01:08:01.220
No way.

1515
01:08:01.400 --> 01:08:01.540
Yeah.

1516
01:08:01.660 --> 01:08:04.240
She's living near JIS, which is where I went to school.

